      "id": 1,
      "text": "Ellendale was named after Ellen Dale Ives, the wife of a railroad official, honoring her humanitarian work.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellendale%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ellendale incorporated in August 1901, opening a post office, mercantile, livery stables, and a stockyard south of the depot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ellendalemn.com/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A two‑story brick school opened in 1910, expanding after 1922 consolidation to accommodate a first graduating class of three in 1923.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ellendalemn.com/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ellendale’s First Lutheran Church, built in 1949, stands on Fifth Street, while the United Methodist Church moved to a new building in 2006.",
